The defect is confirmed in both peers: inbound datagrams call association activation before HEV decode, relay outbound sends can create IDs, and `maxAssociations` is ignored. The clean fix is to separate “validate payload,” “admit client-owned ID,” and “require existing active ID,” with no-state close/error responses for rejected first frames. I’m taking a focused baseline before changing that lifecycle.
