codex
Both state machines now validate HEV bytes before any lifecycle insertion, require active client-owned IDs for relay replies, and reserve association credit before admitting a new ID. Fully retired tombstones are pruned only at admission, keeping the lifecycle map bounded without breaking ordered reuse. I’m compiling the focused suites now, then I’ll update the paired coverage around the new semantics.
